A cozy mountain hut perched on a snowy Alpine hillside at dusk, warm golden light glowing from its windows against the blue twilight snow. In the foreground, a wooden sledge rests half-buried in fresh powder, its runners catching the last light. Pine trees heavy with snow frame the scene, their branches drooping under white weight. The sky transitions from deep purple to pale orange near the horizon where distant peaks create a jagged silhouette. Smoke curls lazily from the hut's chimney, dissipating into the cold air. The entire scene rendered in Vincent van Gogh's distinctive post-impressionist style with bold, swirling brushstrokes in the sky, thick impasto texture on the snow creating dynamic movement, and expressive color contrasts between the warm yellows of the cabin light and the cool blues and purples of the winter evening. The composition conveys the satisfaction of adventure and warmth found after a long climb through harsh conditions.
